<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{@site.locale}}">
<head>

    {{!-- Basic meta only. Open Graph, structured data, canonicals, the
         publisher's accent colour, Members and search all come from
         {{ghost_head}} at the foot of this block — writing any of them by
         hand here means maintaining a copy of something Ghost already
         derives from the content. --}}
    <title>{{meta_title}}</title>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    {{!-- FIRST, and inline: sets data-theme before the first paint. A
         <script src> lands after the page has already painted, which is the
         white-flash-on-every-navigation bug. See the partial. --}}
    {{> "theme-init"}}

    {{!-- The @font-face rules live inside the compiled stylesheet, so the
         browser only discovers them one round trip late. Preloading closes
         that gap, which is what keeps the fallback swap invisible on a cold
         load.

         Only the two faces that draw ABOVE THE FOLD. `crossorigin` is
         required even though these are same-origin — fonts are always
         fetched in CORS mode, and a preload without it produces a second,
         unused download instead of a warm cache hit. --}}
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
          href="{{asset "fonts/switzer-var-latin.woff2"}}">
    <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin
          href="{{asset "fonts/roboto-mono-var-latin.woff2"}}">

    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "built/screen.css"}}">

    {{ghost_head}}

</head>
<body class="{{body_class}}">

    {{!-- FIRST element inside <body>, per NSDS's skip-link archetype. The
         target below needs id="main" AND tabindex="-1" — without the
         tabindex, Safari and Chrome move the viewport but leave focus
         behind, and the link accomplishes nothing. --}}
    <a class="ns-skip-link ns-visually-hidden" href="#main">{{t "Skip to content"}}</a>

    {{!-- ── CHROME DISPATCH ───────────────────────────────────────────────
      A reading surface must not get the marketing bar. Reading kinds carry
      their own chrome inside their own partial — the training rail, the
      course player — so this only decides whether the SITE bar appears.

      ⚠ SKELETON. The tag list below is a placeholder until the collections
      are specified. Each collection gets one file in abstract/collections/,
      and the tag that identifies it is decided there, not here. Adding a
      name to this list before that file exists is how the last content model
      grew by accretion — see abstract/10-how-this-went-wrong.md.
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
    {{#is "post"}}
      {{#post}}
        {{#has tag="#lesson, #docs-page"}}{{else}}{{> "navbar/navbar"}}{{/has}}
      {{/post}}
    {{else}}
      {{> "navbar/navbar"}}
    {{/is}}

    {{> "navbar/sheet"}}

    <main id="main" tabindex="-1">{{{body}}}</main>

    {{#is "post"}}
      {{#post}}
        {{#has tag="#lesson, #docs-page"}}{{else}}{{> "footer/footer"}}{{/has}}
      {{/post}}
    {{else}}
      {{> "footer/footer"}}
    {{/is}}

    {{!-- One bundle, built by gulp from NSDS's own script layer. All of it is
         progressive enhancement: the sheet, the theme controls, the outline,
         the reading line and the code copy button each degrade to something
         that still works. theme-init is deliberately NOT in it. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "built/main.js"}}" defer></script>

    {{ghost_foot}}

</body>
</html>
